[E-TERMINATION] Error: can't show that `rating` terminates
    ╭─[ reject/termination-tuple-match.sw:10:26 ]
    │
 10 │     | (_, Succ later) => rating later numbers
    │                          ──────────┬─────────  
    │                                    ╰─────────── this recursive call might not terminate: the 2nd argument stays the same
    │ 
    │ Note 1: `match (numbers, columns) with` takes apart a tuple built from `numbers` and `columns`, and what its patterns bind isn't seen as a part of `numbers` or `columns`, so it isn't seen as smaller: match them directly, `match numbers, columns with` (without the brackets), or give a measure with `decreasing`
    │ 
    │ Note 2: however the recursive calls are repeated, some argument must get smaller (a part of a pattern-matched constructor); an argument passed on unchanged, or rebuilt from its own pattern, is no smaller
    │ 
    │ Note 3: non-terminating definitions are rejected unless they're partial: `{Partial}` in the result type. A depth limit keeps it total and provable: an extra `fuel: Nat` argument that decreases on each call, failing (or returning a default) when it runs out
────╯
